# CMake and tests

## Module sources

Every new implementation `.cpp` must be added to its own module's `CMakeLists.txt` (`engine/<module>/CMakeLists.txt` or `games/<game>/<sim|app>/CMakeLists.txt`). If it is omitted, the file never compiles.

Each game has an executable `<game>` (`games/<game>/main.cpp`) that links `<game>_app` and `sgl_sfml`. The current games are `arkanoid`, `tetris`, and `syndicate`. Only `sgl_sfml` links SFML, and the executables get it through that link. `<game>_sim` and `<game>_app` stay SFML-free at the include level, and `check_boundaries` enforces this.

## Tests (Debug only)

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

- Unit tests live in `tests/engine/<module>/` and `tests/<game>/<sim|app>/`. GoogleTest 1.18 comes via FetchContent.
- Register each suite with `add_unit_test(...)` in the leaf `CMakeLists.txt`. A new leaf also needs an `add_subdirectory` in `tests/CMakeLists.txt`.
- Tests open no window. `event_translate_test` links `SFML::Window` but opens none.
- Name behavioral fixtures like `*Should`.

When changing a module, update or add unit tests under the matching `tests/engine/<module>/` or `tests/<game>/<sim|app>/` leaf. Recipes are in `docs/how-to/write-headless-tests.md`.
